<title>ARGENTINA: Japanese deputy foreign min. to Argentina, Brazil.</title>
<headline>Japanese deputy foreign min. to Argentina, Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Deputy Foreign Minister Kazuo Ogura arrives in Buenos Aires Thursday to meet President Carlos Menem, on his way to talks with the Mercosur trade bloc in Sao Paulo, the Japanese embassy said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The embassy described the meetings with Mercosur, the customs union grouping Argentina, Brazil, Uruguay and Paraguay that was inaugurated at the beginning of 1995, as the &quot;first chance for Japan and Mercosur to hold high-level talks.&quot;</p>
<p>In Argentina, his visit is aimed at &quot;improving political and economic links&quot; ahead of the 100th anniversary of the first friendship and trade treaty between the two countries.</p>
<p>&quot;Trade and investment issues will be the hot topic, taking into account the development of Mercosur,&quot; the embassy said.</p>
<p>-- Stephen Brown, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695</p>
</text>
